       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.

       PROGRAM-ID.    TCOBERR.
       AUTHOR.        ROGER GLASGOW.
       DATE-WRITTEN.  DEC 1993.

      *D* REMARKS.
      *D*
      *D* ERROR HANDLER FOR COBOL PROGRAMS

      *C
      *C  03/14/97  JEFF BUNGO
      *C  CHANGED THE LOOPING OF RECEIVING MESSAGES TO EXIT FROM
      *C  LOOP AFTER ONE ITERATION IF THE SYSTEM MESSAGE ID IS
      *C  SET TO *NONE.  THIS WILL PREVENT 50 MESSAGES WRITTEN
      *C  WITH THE SAME MESSAGE.


       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES. SYSTEM-CONSOLE IS SYSCON
                      LOCAL-DATA IS LOCAL-DATA-AREA.

      ******************************************************************
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
      ******************************************************************
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT ERROR-FILE
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFPERRORS
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT MSG-ID-FILE
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFPMSGIDS
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.


      ******************************************************************
       DATA DIVISION.
      ******************************************************************

       FILE SECTION.
       FD  ERROR-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  ERROR-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFPERRORS.

       FD  MSG-ID-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSG-ID-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFPMSGIDS.

      ******************************************************************
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
      ******************************************************************
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  M E S S A G E S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  ERR-MSG.
           05                                   PIC X(44)
               VALUE "An error has occurred and has been recorded.".
           05                                   PIC X(14)  VALUE SPACES.
           05                                   PIC X      VALUE "(".
           05  ERR-MSG-COBOL-ID                 PIC X(7).
           05                                   PIC X      VALUE ":".
           05  ERR-MSG-SYSTEM-ID                PIC X(7).
           05                                   PIC X      VALUE ":".
           05  ERR-MSG-PROGNAME                 PIC X(10).
           05                                   PIC X      VALUE ")".

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  F L A G S   A N D   S W I T C H E S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  SWITCHES-AREA.
           03  SW-OFF                        PIC 1  VALUE B"0".
           03  SW-ON                         PIC 1  VALUE B"1".

       01  MESSAGES-SW                       PIC 1.
               88  END-OF-MESSAGES VALUE B"1".

       01  MESSAGE-ID                        PIC X(7).

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  I N D E X E S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  SUB                               PIC S9(3)  COMP-3.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  M I S C E L L A N E O U S   D A T E   &   T I M E   F I E L D S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  CUR-DATE                          PIC X(6).
       01  CUR-TIME                          PIC X(6).

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  D A T A B A S E   S T A T U S   A R E A
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  FILE-STATUS.
           05  FILE-STATUS-1                 PIC X.
           05  FILE-STATUS-2                 PIC X.

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  U T I L I T Y   A R E A
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION               PIC X(200).

       01  JOB-ATTRIBUTES.
           05  JOB-NAME                          PIC X(10).
           05  JOB-USER                          PIC X(10).
           05  JOB-NUM                           PIC X(6).
           05  JOB-GRPPRF                        PIC X(10).
           05  JOB-MSGQ                          PIC X(10).
           05  JOB-MSGID                         PIC X(7).

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  D A T A B A S E   A N D   F I L E   B U F F E R S
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------

       01  RECEIVE-MESSAGE-API-PARAMETERS.
           05  API-MESSAGE.
               10  API-BYTES-RETURNED            PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-BYTES-AVAILABLE           PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-SEVERITY          PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-IDENTIFIER        PIC X(7).
               10  API-MESSAGE-TYPE-A            PIC X(2).
               10  API-MESSAGE-KEY-A             PIC X(4).
               10  API-MESSAGE-FILE              PIC X(10).
               10  API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB          PIC X(10).
               10  API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB-USED     PIC X(10).
               10  API-SENDING-JOB               PIC X(10).
               10  API-SENDING-USER-PROFILE      PIC X(10).
               10  API-SENDING-JOB-NUMBER        PIC X(6).
               10  API-SENDING-PROGRAM           PIC X(12).
               10  API-SENDING-PROGRAM-INST      PIC X(4).
               10  API-DATE-SENT                 PIC X(7).
               10  API-TIME-SENT                 PIC X(6).
               10  API-RECEIVING-PROGRAM         PIC X(10).
               10  API-RECEIVING-PROGRAM-INST    PIC X(4).
               10  FILLER                        PIC X(11).
               10  API-ALERT-OPTION              PIC X(9).
               10  FILLER                        PIC X(8).
               10  API-MESSAGE-DATA-LENGTH       PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-DATA-AVAIL        PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-A          PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-AVAIL      PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-HELP-LENGTH       PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-HELP-AVAIL        PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-MESSAGE-TEXT              PIC X(100).
               10  API-MESSAGE-HELP              PIC X(100).
           05  API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-B              PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
           05  API-FORMAT                        PIC X(8).
           05  API-PROGRAM-MESSAGE-QUEUE         PIC X(20).
           05  API-PROGRAM-STACK-COUNTER         PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
           05  API-MESSAGE-TYPE-B                PIC X(10).
           05  API-MESSAGE-KEY-B                 PIC X(4).
           05  API-WAIT-TIME                     PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
           05  API-MESSAGE-ACTION                PIC X(10).
           05  API-ERROR.
               10  API-BYTES-IN                  PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-BYTES-OUT                 PIC 9(5) COMP-4.
               10  API-EXCEPTION-ID              PIC X(7).
               10  API-RESERVED                  PIC X.
               10  API-ADDITIONAL                PIC X(100).

       01  BUF-MSG-ID.
           05  MSG-MAIN-ID                       PIC X(10).
           05  MSG-SUB-ID                        PIC X(10).
           05  MSG-RTN-CODE                      PIC X.
           05  MSG-DSP-SCRMSG                    PIC X.
           05  MSG-DSP-JOBLOG                    PIC X.
           05  MSG-DSP-JOB                       PIC X.
           05  MSG-RTV-ERR-MSG                   PIC X.
           05  MSG-SUBPGM-ERR                    PIC X.
           05  MSG-SUBPGM-MSG                    PIC X(100).

      ******************************************************************
       LINKAGE SECTION.
      ******************************************************************

       01  COBOL-ID                          PIC X(7).
       01  VALID-RESPONSES                   PIC X(6).
       01  PROGR.
            05  PROGNAME                     PIC X(10).
            05  PROGLIBR                     PIC X(10).
       01  SYSTEM-ID                         PIC X(7).
       01  LEN-TEXT                          PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  SUBTEXT.
           03  SUBCHARS                      PIC X
               OCCURS 1 TO 230 TIMES DEPENDING ON LEN-TEXT.
       01  RETCODE                           PIC X(1).

      ******************************************************************
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING COBOL-ID,  VALID-RESPONSES,   PROGR,
                                SYSTEM-ID, SUBTEXT, LEN-TEXT, RETCODE.
      ******************************************************************

      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
       000-MAIN.
      *-----------------------------------------------------------------
           OPEN I-O   ERROR-FILE.
           OPEN INPUT MSG-ID-FILE.
           ACCEPT CUR-DATE                    FROM DATE.
           ACCEPT CUR-TIME                    FROM TIME.
           CALL "UTX9001A" USING JOB-NAME
                                 JOB-USER
                                 JOB-NUM
                                 JOB-GRPPRF
                                 JOB-MSGQ
                                 JOB-MSGID.

      *    DISPLAY "COBOL ID: " COBOL-ID.
      *    DISPLAY "VALID RESPONSES: " VALID-RESPONSES.
      *    DISPLAY "PROGRAM NAME: " PROGNAME.
      *    DISPLAY "LIBRARY NAME: " PROGLIBR.
      *    DISPLAY "SYSTEM ID: " SYSTEM-ID.
      *    DISPLAY "LENGTH OF TEXT: " LEN-TEXT.
      *    DISPLAY "TEXT: " SUBTEXT.
      *    DISPLAY "RETURN CODE: " RETCODE.

           PERFORM 100-EVALUATE-ERROR        THRU 100-EXIT.

           PERFORM 010-EOJ.

       010-EOJ.
           CLOSE ERROR-FILE.
           EXIT PROGRAM.

       100-EVALUATE-ERROR.

      *----SET UP ERROR KEY.

           MOVE COBOL-ID     TO MAINID.
           IF(COBOL-ID = "LBE7204" OR "LBE7212")AND PROGNAME = "TBLOWUP"
              MOVE PROGNAME  TO SUBID
           ELSE
              MOVE SYSTEM-ID TO SUBID.

      *----TRY TO FIND THE RECORD USING MAIN AND SUB ID'S.

           READ MSG-ID-FILE INTO BUF-MSG-ID
              INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.

      *----IF NOT THERE, USE JUST MAIN ID.

           IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
              MOVE SPACES TO SUBID
              READ MSG-ID-FILE INTO BUF-MSG-ID
                 INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS
              END-READ

      *-------IF NOT THERE, USE DEFAULT RECORD

              IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
                 MOVE "DEFAULT" TO MAINID
                 MOVE "DEFAULT" TO SUBID
                 READ MSG-ID-FILE INTO BUF-MSG-ID

      *----------------IF CAN'T READ FILE, USE FOLLOWING DEFAULTS

                    INVALID KEY
                       INITIALIZE BUF-MSG-ID
                       MOVE "C" TO MSG-RTN-CODE
                       MOVE "Y" TO MSG-DSP-SCRMSG
                       MOVE "Y" TO MSG-DSP-JOBLOG
                       MOVE "N" TO MSG-DSP-JOB
                       MOVE "Y" TO MSG-RTV-ERR-MSG
                       MOVE "N" TO MSG-SUBPGM-ERR
                       MOVE SPACES TO MSG-SUBPGM-MSG.

           IF MSG-DSP-SCRMSG = "Y"
              MOVE COBOL-ID TO ERR-MSG-COBOL-ID
              MOVE SYSTEM-ID TO ERR-MSG-SYSTEM-ID
              MOVE PROGNAME TO ERR-MSG-PROGNAME
              DISPLAY ERR-MSG.
           MOVE MSG-RTN-CODE TO RETCODE.
           IF MSG-SUBPGM-ERR = "Y"
              PERFORM 300-WRITE-MORE-INFO THRU 300-EXIT.
           IF MSG-RTV-ERR-MSG = "Y"
              PERFORM 200-RETRIEVE-MESSAGES THRU 200-EXIT.
           IF MSG-DSP-JOBLOG = "Y"
              CALL "MCXDSPJBLG".
           IF MSG-DSP-JOB = "Y"
              CALL "MCXDSPJOB".

       100-EXIT.  EXIT.

       200-RETRIEVE-MESSAGES.
           MOVE SW-OFF                       TO MESSAGES-SW.
           MOVE SPACES                       TO MESSAGE-ID.
           PERFORM 210-PROCESS-MESSAGES      THRU 210-EXIT VARYING
               SUB FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL SUB > 50 OR
               SYSTEM-ID EQUAL MESSAGE-ID OR
               END-OF-MESSAGES.

       200-EXIT.  EXIT.

       210-PROCESS-MESSAGES.
           MOVE 116                       TO API-BYTES-IN.
           MOVE 376                       TO API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-B.
           MOVE "RCVM0200"                TO API-FORMAT.
           MOVE "TCOBERR"                 TO API-PROGRAM-MESSAGE-QUEUE.
           MOVE 2                         TO API-PROGRAM-STACK-COUNTER.
           IF SUB = 1
               MOVE "*FIRST "             TO API-MESSAGE-TYPE-B
               MOVE SPACES                TO API-MESSAGE-KEY-B
           ELSE
               MOVE "*NEXT  "             TO API-MESSAGE-TYPE-B
               MOVE API-MESSAGE-KEY-A     TO API-MESSAGE-KEY-B.
           MOVE ZERO                      TO API-WAIT-TIME.
           MOVE "*OLD"                    TO API-MESSAGE-ACTION.
           CALL "QMHRCVPM" USING API-MESSAGE
                                 API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-B
                                 API-FORMAT
                                 API-PROGRAM-MESSAGE-QUEUE
                                 API-PROGRAM-STACK-COUNTER
                                 API-MESSAGE-TYPE-B
                                 API-MESSAGE-KEY-B
                                 API-WAIT-TIME
                                 API-MESSAGE-ACTION
                                 API-ERROR.
           IF API-MESSAGE-KEY-A EQUAL SPACES
               MOVE SW-ON                 TO MESSAGES-SW.
           IF API-EXCEPTION-ID EQUAL SPACES AND
              API-MESSAGE-IDENTIFIER NOT EQUAL SPACES
               CALL "MCXRTVMSG" USING API-MESSAGE-IDENTIFIER
                                      API-MESSAGE-FILE
                                      API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB
                                      API-MESSAGE-TEXT
                                      MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION
               MOVE API-MESSAGE-TEXT (1:7)    TO MESSAGE-ID
      *        IF SYSTEM-ID NOT = "CPF9846"
      *           DISPLAY "MESSAGE IDENTIFIER: " API-MESSAGE-IDENTIFIER
      *        END-IF
      *        DISPLAY "MESSAGE DATA: " API-MESSAGE-TEXT
      *        DISPLAY "MESSAGE DESCRIPTION: " MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION
      *        DISPLAY "MESSAGE FILE: " API-MESSAGE-FILE
      *        DISPLAY "MESSAGE FILE LIBRARY: " API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB
      *        DISPLAY "LENGTH OF MESSAGE TEXT: " API-MESSAGE-LENGTH-A
      *        DISPLAY "SENDING JOB: " API-SENDING-JOB
      *        DISPLAY "SENDING USER PROFILE: " API-SENDING-USER-PROFILE
      *        DISPLAY "SENDING JOB NUMBER: " API-SENDING-JOB-NUMBER
      *        DISPLAY "SENDING PROGRAM: " API-SENDING-PROGRAM
      *        DISPLAY "SENDING PROGRAM INSTRUCTION: "
      *                                    API-SENDING-PROGRAM-INST
      *        DISPLAY "DATE SENT: " API-DATE-SENT
      *        DISPLAY "TIME SENT: " API-TIME-SENT
      *        DISPLAY "RECEIVING PROGRAM: " API-RECEIVING-PROGRAM
      *        DISPLAY "RECEIVING PROGRAM INSTRUCTION: "
      *                                 API-RECEIVING-PROGRAM-INST
               MOVE CUR-DATE                  TO MCDATE
               MOVE CUR-TIME                  TO MCTIME
               MOVE JOB-USER                  TO MCUSER
               MOVE JOB-NAME                  TO MCJOB
               MOVE JOB-NUM                   TO MCNBR
               MOVE PROGNAME                  TO MCPGM
               MOVE PROGLIBR                  TO MCLIB
               MOVE API-MESSAGE-IDENTIFIER    TO MCMSG
               MOVE MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION       TO MCDESC
               IF API-MESSAGE-SEVERITY > 30
                  PERFORM 400-WRITE-ERROR.
           IF SYSTEM-ID = "*NONE"
               MOVE SW-ON                 TO MESSAGES-SW.

       210-EXIT.  EXIT.

       300-WRITE-MORE-INFO.
           MOVE CUR-DATE                     TO MCDATE.
           MOVE CUR-TIME                     TO MCTIME.
           MOVE JOB-USER                     TO MCUSER.
           MOVE JOB-NAME                     TO MCJOB.
           MOVE JOB-NUM                      TO MCNBR.
           MOVE PROGNAME                     TO MCPGM.
           MOVE PROGLIBR                     TO MCLIB.
           MOVE COBOL-ID                     TO MCMSG.
           MOVE MSG-SUBPGM-MSG               TO MCDESC.

           PERFORM 400-WRITE-ERROR.

           MOVE "QCPFMSG"                TO API-MESSAGE-FILE.
           MOVE "QSYS"                   TO API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB.
           MOVE SUBTEXT                  TO API-MESSAGE-TEXT.
           CALL "MCXRTVMSG" USING SYSTEM-ID
                                  API-MESSAGE-FILE
                                  API-MESSAGE-FILE-LIB
                                  API-MESSAGE-TEXT
                                  MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION.
           MOVE SYSTEM-ID                 TO MCMSG.
           MOVE MESSAGE-DESCRIPTION       TO MCDESC.

           PERFORM 400-WRITE-ERROR.

       300-EXIT.  EXIT.

       400-WRITE-ERROR.
           WRITE ERROR-REC.
           IF FILE-STATUS NOT EQUAL ZERO
              DISPLAY "Error Writing MCFPERRORS: " FILE-STATUS.

